/**

\page examples Example programs

The programs in \c test/ are built with the library.

\section examples_dock dock

\c dock.cxx is a demonstration of every feature: an OpenGL view in the
center and panels around it, stripes of buttons on every side, a GL panel
whose stripe button has an icon, a panel that asks before it closes, one
that cannot be closed, one created only when it is first asked for, two
editors that start closed and take turns in one place, menus for the
panels, whole-dock commands, the stripes' options and saved layouts, and a
log of what the dock's callback reports.

\section examples_tests Tests

  - \c unittest_dock.cxx tests the tree, drop targets, floating, inset and
    sliding windows, stripes, layouts, the callback and the event dispatch,
    and every public function.
  - \c gl_dock.cxx checks that OpenGL views keep drawing as the center and
    in panels that are floated, docked, moved, closed and shown.
  - \c window_dock.cxx checks a dock's windows as the application's window
    is shown and closed.

Run them with \c ctest.  \c gl_dock and \c window_dock are labeled
\c display, as they need one; on X11 and Wayland \c unittest_dock needs
one too, to measure text.

*/
